---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import { checkedAgainst } from '../data/app';
import { contributingUrl, pullUrl } from '../data/links';
---
<Base title="Contributors" checked={checkedAgainst}>
  <div class="page">
    <div>
      <h1>Who made Sudo Hire?</h1>
      <div class="answer">
        <p>Sudo Hire is open source, under the MIT license. These people contributed to it.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="alberto-arena">Alberto Arena</h2>
      <p>Alberto Arena created Sudo Hire and maintains it. On GitHub: <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/albertoarena">@albertoarena</ExternalLink>.</p>

      <h2 id="daniele-barbaro">Daniele Barbaro</h2>
      <p>On GitHub: <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/danielebarbaro">@danielebarbaro</ExternalLink>.</p>
      <p>His work is in Sudo Hire since v1.1.0:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>He wrote the Workable reader. With it, Sudo Hire reads the career pages of companies that use Workable (<ExternalLink href={`${pullUrl}/55`}>pull request 55</ExternalLink>).</li>
        <li>He checked the terms of Workable for this reader.</li>
        <li>He researched how Workable companies list the countries of remote jobs. The research set which remote Workable jobs show a country.</li>
        <li>He made Sudo Hire read the Lever companies of the EU instance (<ExternalLink href={`${pullUrl}/57`}>pull request 57</ExternalLink>).</li>
        <li>He made a company name leave out a domain ending: jimdo.com shows as “Jimdo” (<ExternalLink href={`${pullUrl}/56`}>pull request 56</ExternalLink>).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>He also wrote connectors for more career page providers, under the MIT license: <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/plin-code/job-boards-smartrecruiters">job-boards-smartrecruiters</ExternalLink> and <ExternalLink href="https://github.com/plin-code/job-boards-bamboohr">job-boards-bamboohr</ExternalLink>.</p>

      <h2 id="contribute">How can I contribute?</h2>
      <p>Read <ExternalLink href={contributingUrl}>CONTRIBUTING.md</ExternalLink> in sudo-hire. Each person who contributes is named on this page.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
